    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5352111/assistant-associate-professor-md6-course-director-0088902t-readvertisement": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director, 0088902T) READVERTISEMENT Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Kaka'ako - Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01062 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Division Associate Dean for Academic Affairs Opening Date 06/29/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0088902T Description Title: Assistant/Associate Professor (MD6 Course Director) Position Number: 0088902T Hiring Unit: John A. Burns School of Medicine – Office of Medical Education Location: John A Burns School of Medicine, Medical Education Building Date Posted: 6/29/2026 Closing Date: Continuous, First review on 7/14/2026 Salary Information: Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. Monthly Type: 11 Month Tenure Track: Non-Tenure Full Time/Part Time: Part Time - Full Time Equivalency: 25% Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: To begin approximately July 2026 subject to position clearance and availability of funds. Position is renewable subject to performance and/or funding availability. Duties & Responsibilities: Serve as one of the co-course directors for the MD6 (Neuro/Locomotor/Behavioral) curricular unit. Plan and implement the contents and activities for the course, including PBL case development and modification. Appropriately assess student performance and provide necessary student remediation. Ensure that all aspects of the course are in-line with JABSOM's educational philosophy and advance students towards achievement of the JABSOM graduation objectives. Recruit, orient, and facilitate evaluation of PBL tutors. Participate as a member of the JABSOM pre-clinical education committee. Maintain and update the curriculum map and content maps related to the course. Recruit speakers for course lectures/seminars/workshops, work with OME staff to schedule sessions and communicate with speakers, and help to facilitate speaker evaluations. Assign tasks to supervise and evaluate Junior Course Directors assigned to their course. Facilitate PBL sessions as a tutor in at least one MD unit during the academic year. Contributes to the mission of the Office of Medical Education in the areas of faculty development, community service, and community outreach. Contributes to the preparation for LCME accreditation. Attend and participate in functions required of all OME faculty, such as Medical Education Grand Rounds, Faculty Meetings, and Convocation. Participate or lead educational task forces under the Office of Medical Education, the Curriculum Committee, or another educational subcommittee. Provide lectures or conferences/colloquia upon request. Evidence of effective teaching is required. This includes evidence of facilitating student-centered learning and demonstration of a positive attitude to student growth. Serve on JABSOM and/or University committees. Conduct scholarly work in medical education which may include research or curriculum descriptions. The scholarly work should be published and/or presented at peer-reviewed forums. Other duties as assigned (includes but not limited to participating in community engagement activities, directing office initiatives, etc.) Minimum Qualifications: Assistant Professor: M.D. or D.O. degree or equivalent medical degree from an accredited medical school. Relevant board certification in or qualification in the clinical discipline of the specific position. Demonstrated clinical and/or educational expertise in one or more of the following areas: neurology, musculoskeletal/sports medicine, or psychiatry Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others Excellent organizational skills Evidence of effective teaching Demonstrated potential for research/scholarship Experience using teaching methods such as problem-based learning, team-based learning, project-based learning, or another method that emphasizes active, self-directed learning Associate Professor: Same as Assistant Plus... In the rank of Assistant Professor, or four years of other health care experience, or a total of four years of teaching in the rank of Assistant Professor and other experience, or on year at the rank of Associate Professor at another health care school of recognized .standing . Proven ability in teaching, research, and program administration. Recognition for having made a significant scholarly contribution to the clinical specialty. Ability to serve as a role model for students and junior colleagues. Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others. Desirable Qualifications Three (3) years of experience in medical student education Teaching evaluations that attest to creative and innovative teaching methods that are well-received by students Demonstrated ability to work and teach collaboratively with other faculty within and across disciplines Comfortable working in a multi-cultural setting To Apply: Applicants must submit the following electronically via Work at UH: cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; current Curriculum Vitae; names and contact information of five (5) professional references, and official transcripts or original documentation from the institution confirming degree or copy of U.S. board certification or U.S. medical license (copies of transcripts are accepted when used in lieu of current U.S. board certification or current U.S. medical license, however, if used for verification, original transcripts sent directly from the degree granting institution is required upon hire). Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Inquiries: Maria Uyeunten - monsell@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus- security/, or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case- by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5250781/assistant-associate-professor-marine-biologist-0082434": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Marine Biologist (0082434)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Marine Biologist (0082434) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-00338 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Natural Sciences - School of Life Sciences Opening Date 02/25/2026 Position Number: 0082434 Description Title: Assistant / Associate Professor (Marine Biologist) Position Numbers: 0082434 Hiring Unit: College of Natural Sciences - School of Life Sciences Location: Manoa Date Posted: February 25, 2026 Closing Date: Application review begins March 19, 2026 Salary Information: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Monthly Type: 9 Month Tenure Track: Tenure Full/Part Time: Full time Temp/Perm: Permanent Funding: General Funds Position Description The School of Life Sciences (SoLS) at the University of Hawai‘i at Manoa seeks a candidate for an Assistant (F3) or Associate Professor (F4) of Marine Biology position who uses integrative approaches to investigate the underlying mechanisms of responses of marine organisms, populations, or communities to environmental change. Research should connect organismal biology and ecology, and may integrate multiple biological, spatial, and/or temporal scales. Research that will focus on Hawaiian species is of particular interest. The successful candidate can have research experience in any area of marine biology, including but not limited to physiological, ecological, and/or evolutionary approaches. This is a permanent, tenure-track, full-time, 9-month facutly appointment to begin August 1, 2026, subject to position clearance, availability of funds and satisfactory performance. The University of Hawai‘i at Manoa (UHM) is a Carnegie Research 1 University with strong emphases on research and undergraduate and graduate education. Our campus welcomes all students but given our responsibilities to the community in which we operate, as part of our strategic mission, we strive to become a Native Hawaiian Place of Learning, a place that is committed to integrating Native Hawaiian language, culture and/or values into its academic and campus environment. Our vision is to be locally and globally recognized as a premier student-centered and community-serving university ( https://manoa.hawaii.edu/strategicplan/) . The School of Life Sciences hosts the largest academic program on the University of Hawai‘i’s flagship campus, serving over 1,500 undergraduate majors and 150 graduate students for degrees in biology, botany, marine biology, microbiology, molecular cell biology, and zoology. Research interests of the 40 faculty members span all biological scales, with many focusing on ecology, evolution, and conservation biology. The School of Life Sciences is committed to serving our community and state and to excellence in research and teaching. ( https://manoa.hawaii.edu/lifesciences/) . Assistant Professor Duties and Responsibilities - Develop and sustain an innovative, externally funded research program - Mentor and advise graduate and undergraduate students in the School of Life Sciences - Provide high-quality teaching in support of the Marine Biology B.S. and B.A. degree programs - Develop and teach graduate courses in their area of expertise that directly contribute to one or more of the graduate degrees offered by the School of Life Sciences - Serve on departmental, college, and university committees as appropriate - Render service to the professional and local/regional community that is relevant to the individual’s academic specialty Associate Professor Duties and Responsibilities - In addition to the duties and responsibilities associated with the Assistant Professor rank, the role encompasses leadership at the University and national levels. Assistant Professor Minimum Qualifications - A Ph.D or equivalent terminal degree from a college or university of recognized standing in a field relevant to the position. - Research experience in marine biology or a related field - Excellence and creativity in research, as demonstrated by publications in peer-reviewed journals - Ability to teach and mentor students of various backgrounds in core classes in the Marine Biology major, such as algal diversity, invertebrate biology, fish biology, marine microbiology, marine ecology and evolution, or an advanced capstone course, among others - Commitment to supporting the key principles of the School of Life Sciences, which include personal and professional integrity, and the pursuit of excellence in instruction and research - Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others. Associate Professor Minimum Qualifications In addition to those of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor minimum qualifications include: - Four years in the rank of Assistant Professor - Documented participation in the scholarly and academic affairs of their Department, University, or professional organization - Clear recognition among peers at the local and/or regional levels Assistant Professor Desirable Qualifications - Postdoctoral research experience - Evidence of external research funding - Demonstrated experience and excellence in instruction of undergraduate and graduate students in the life sciences, with an emphasis on marine biology - Experience working with students of various backgrounds and various community populations - Vision of research that takes advantage of Hawai‘i’s unique location, resources, and faculty expertise in the School of Life Sciences, other university units, and state and federal agencies engaged in marine research - Connection to global change issues Associate Professor Desirable Qualifications In addition to those of Assistant Professor, Associate Processor desirable qualifications include: - Departmental leadership experience - Demonstrated record of excellent evaluations on teaching of students and other trainees - Scientific peer-reviewed publication in major journals related to their field To Apply Applicants should submit: 1) a cover letter in which you identify the position for which you are applying and indicate how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of research interests, activities, and plans (up to 3 pages in length); 4) a statement of teaching philosophy, interests, and plans (up to 2 pages in length); 5) copies of up to three relevant publications; and 6) names and contact information (including email addresses and telephone numbers) for three professional references. Additional information about Manoa’s Strategic Vision as a Native Hawaiian place of learning can be found here: https://manoa.hawaii.edu/strategicplan/ . Official transcripts with proof of degree conferred will be required upon hire. Inquiries: Dr. Megan Porter, mlporter@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5531225/assistant-associate-professor-in-safe-and-trustworthy-ai-systems": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Safe and Trustworthy AI Systems",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Safe and Trustworthy AI Systems Salary $0.00 Semi-Monthly Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 0084029-02 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Natural Sciences - ICS Opening Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0084029 Description Title: Assistant or Associate Professor in Safe and Trustworthy AI Systems Hiring Unit: College of Natural Sciences, Information & Computer Sciences Department Position: 0084029 Location: Manoa Campus Date Posted: October 27, 2026 Closing Date : Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Salary Information: Commensurate with qualifications and experience Monthly Type: 9-Month Tenure Track: Tenure Full-Time/Part-Time: Full-Time Temporary/Permanent: Permanent The Department of Information and Computer Sciences (ICS) at the University of Hawai?i at Manoa invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position in Safe and Trustworthy AI Systems, beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year. This position is part of a three-position cluster focused on Human-First AI that also includes two Assistant Professor positions, one in AI Computing and one in Agentic AI and Autonomous Systems. Each position is a separate search. Candidates who wish to be considered for more than one position must submit a separate application for each. The cluster hire aims to advance research in AI agents, AI computing systems, and AI safety. The candidate will contribute to the department’s growing AI curriculum, the proposed BS in Computer Science Artificial Intelligence Track, and the Professional MCS in AI/Data Science. This position will be connected to the new University of Hawai?i AI Institute currently under development. The Institute’s mission is to advance human-first AI through research, education, and service that strengthen the capabilities and well-being of Hawai?i’s people, with human judgment and decision-making, responsible stewardship, and community-defined priorities guiding its work. Research Focus We seek candidates who advance the foundations, methods, and computing systems needed for safe, trustworthy, resilient, and human-first AI. Areas of interest include AI safety and alignment; security and privacy of AI models, privacy-preserving AI systems; verification, validation, and monitoring; dependable embedded and edge AI; resilient cyber-physical and intelligent sensing systems; and human-centered evaluation and responsible deployment. Contributions may address ethical, legal, and societal implications of AI and malicious attacks, failures, uncertainty, or resource constraints through AI methods, enabling computing systems, or their integration. Duties and Responsibilities Teach and develop undergraduate and graduate courses in the candidate’s area of expertise and related areas of artificial intelligence, as well as other courses in information and computer sciences Establish or sustain an extramurally funded research program; publish high-quality scholarly work Supervise graduate research Mentor and advise undergraduate Participate in capstone mentoring; develop interdisciplinary and external collaborations Provide department, college, and university service; and Perform other scholarly duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field by the start date. Evidence of high-quality research through peer-reviewed publications in conferences or journals relevant to the position sought. Commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching, mentoring, and advising. Demonstrated ability to collaborate with diverse groups of students, faculty, and external partners. For Assistant Professor appointments: strong potential to establish an independent research program and obtain extramural funding. For Associate Professor consideration: an established independent research program, sustained scholarly contributions and extramural funding, and a record of effective teaching, student mentoring, and service appropriate to the rank. Desirable Qualifications Experience developing or evaluating AI methods or computing systems relevant to this position, including efficient AI computing, agents that plan and use tools, or systems operating under safety, security, reliability, privacy, or resource constraints. Experience translating research into usable tools, models, software, platforms, benchmarks, or evaluation methods, with attention to accessibility, meaningful human control, and impacts on users and communities. Experience with interdisciplinary or applied research involving government, industry, or nonprofit partners. Experience mentoring students from a variety of backgrounds and disciplines through research, internships, or collaborative projects. About the University The University of Hawai?i at Manoa is the flagship campus of the UH system and the only R1 university in the state. It is dedicated to teaching, research, and service in a multicultural and inclusive environment. Appointment Conditions Pending position clearance. This is an Assistant or Associate Professor search; rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience and subject to applicable University appointment requirements. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. How to Apply Apply through the posting for this position and submit the following materials with your application: A cover letter identifying this position and explaining how you satisfy the relevant minimum and desirable qualifications. Candidates applying to multiple searches may also indicate their interest in the other positions. A curriculum vitae with a publication list. Names and contact information for three individuals willing to provide professional reference letters. A statement of research interests, accomplishments, and future research plans. A statement describing your experience and approach to teaching and mentoring, including any experience mentoring projects with industry or other external partners. Candidates whose expertise spans more than one area are encouraged to apply to each relevant position and indicate that interest in their cover letter. Applications will be evaluated separately against the qualifications of each position. Where permitted, interviews and campus visits may be coordinated across searches. Application materials will not be returned. Incomplete applications will not be accepted. Inquiries: Guylaine Poisson, guylaine@hawaii.edu (Department Chair) EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5504473/assistant-associate-professor-f3-f4-9-mo-faculty": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, (F3/F4) 9-mo.- Faculty",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, (F3/F4) 9-mo.- Faculty Salary $0.00 Semi-Monthly Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Honolulu, HI Job Type Full-Time Permanent Job Number 2026-02097 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Division Anatomy, Biochemistry, and Physiology Opening Date 10/02/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description AMENDED Position Title: Assistant/Associate Professor, (F3/F4) 9-mo.- Faculty Position #: Pending Hiring Unit: UHM John A. Burns School of Medicine (JABSOM), Department of Anatomy, Biochemistry and Physiology (ABP), Yanagimachi Institute for Biogenesis Research Location: Yanagimachi Institute for Biogenesis Research (YIBR), UHM campus Date Posted: October 2, 2026 Closing Date: Continuous recruitment until position is filled, first review updated from October 19, 2026 to October 26, 2026 Salary Information: Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience Monthly Type: 9-month Tenure Track: Tenure-track Full Time/Part Time: Full Time, 100% FTE Temporary/Permanent: Permanent Funding: General Other Conditions: To begin approximately January 2027. Renewal dependent upon performance. Assistant Professor Duties and Responsibilities: The University of Hawaii Yanagimachi Institute for Biogenesis Research (YIBR) is seeking a scholarly individual with a strong and documented commitment to research, teaching, and service that will be a role model and mentor for our learners and colleagues. Performing Scholarly Activities (60% Research) Carry out original research in reproductive biology. Acquire and maintain competitive federal, intramural, and other grant funding to support research activities. Publish scholarly, peer-reviewed research in the field of reproductive biology Present research results at the professional conferences locally, nationally and/or internationally. Actively collaborate with faculty, fellows, students, and other research partners within YIBR, JABSOM, and health care industry/community in Hawaii? Collaborate with other faculty from ABP and JABSOM to advance the research mission of the YIBR. Establish and build on a national reputation through steady flow of scholarly, peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, and similar activities. Other scholarly duties as assigned. Teaching (20% Teaching) Teach undergraduate and/or graduate credit-bearing courses based on department needs and priorities. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students, medical students, postdoctoral scholars, and residents. Serve as an academic advisor to undergraduate, MS, and PhD students. Administration (20% Service) Participate in YIBR, ABP, JABSOM and/or University-wide committees, including serving on graduate committees, department and university committees, and the faculty senate. Contribute to committees and service activities in the field at the national level. Associate Professor Duties and Responsibilities: 60% Research, 20% Teaching, 20% Service In addition to the duties and responsibilities for the Assistant Professor rank, assume leadership roles in research, teaching and service. Specifically, direct or administer programs in research with national/international collaborations, develop and instruct a new graduate level course, and expand service activities at local and national/international levels. Assistant Professor Minimum Qualifications: PhD or equivalent terminal degree in biological sciences or relevant field, from an accredited college or university of recognized standing. OD/MD from an accredited college or university of recognized standing would be also considered. One to three years of post-doctoral experience performing research in the general area of reproductive biology Demonstrated ability to effectively conduct research and scholarly activities in the reproductive biology field, including scientific publications in peer-reviewed journals, conference presentations, etc. Ability and commitment to mentoring and training undergraduate and graduate students, and post-docs. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work in a collaborative environment. Poise and good address for meeting and conferring with others. Associate Professor Minimum Qualifications: Same as Assistant Professor with the additional minimum qualifications below. Minimum of four (4) years of full-time service at college or university at the rank of Assistant Professor Demonstrated experience with leading an independent laboratory with research focus on general area of reproductive biology. Demonstrated grantsmanship evidenced as independently acquired NIH R01 or other equivalent federal/state or private funding. Demonstrated scholarly achievements commensurate with rank. Demonstrated proficiency in teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level. Assistant Professor Desirable Qualifications: First and senior/corresponding author of papers in high-quality journals. Demonstrated ability to obtain extramural funding as evidenced by prior NIH or other federal/state or private funding. Current federal funding support with an NIH R01 or K award or the equivalent level of extramural grants. Recognition of having made a major contribution to the reproductive biology field. Recognition among peers at the local, regional, and/or national levels. Evidence of strong research/scholarship productivity. Evidence of strong proficiency in teaching. Evidence of leadership in academic setting and/or reproductive biology field. Demonstrated ability to lead a research laboratory. Teaching experiences with undergraduate, graduate and/or medical students Associate Professor Desirable Qualifications: Same as Assistant Professor with the additional desirable qualifications below. Senior authorship of papers in prestigious peer-reviewed journals. Active current external support (NIH R01 level or equivalent). National recognition for independent contribution to the reproductive biology field. Serving on NIH study section or equivalent. Specialization in a reproductive biology research area. To Apply: Click on the “Apply button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach the required documents before the closing date: Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications and describing research interests and teaching philosophy; Current Curriculum Vitae; *Official transcripts of the highest educational degree earned that is relevant to this position from the institution confirming degree (copies acceptable; however official transcripts sent directly from the degree granting institution required upon hire); Copies of all licenses and certificates; Five (5) professional references (include contact information with email address). *Official transcripts sent directly from the degree granting institution is required upon hire. Transcripts issued outside of the United States of America require a course-by-course analysis verifying the degree equivalency to that of an accredited institution within the USA, from an agency having membership with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). Applicant is responsible for expense of evaluation. Original documentation from the institution confirming degree; Please note that incomplete application will not be considered. The application will be incomplete if materials are unreadable, illegible, password protected, missing or corrupted; therefor, late or incomplete application will not be considered. NOTE: If you have not applied for a position before using NEOGOV, you will need to create an account. All application material should be uploaded to this website and not to the email listed below. Please be sure you are including all required documents as stated above. If you need to make any changes to your application, you will need to reapply and attach the documents again Inquiries: Dr. Monika Ward (mward@hawaii.edu) EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5537813/assistant-associate-professor-h3-h4-hem-onc-core-88696t-88795t": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, H3/H4 (Hem/Onc Core - 88696T & 88795T)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, H3/H4 (Hem/Onc Core - 88696T & 88795T) Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Queen's Medical Center - Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-02344 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Division Medicine Opening Date 11/02/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 88696T & 88795T Description Title: Assistant/Associate Professor, H3/H4 (Hematology / Oncology Core) Position #: 88696T & 88795T (2 positions) Hiring Unit: Department of Medicine Location: Queen’s University Tower Campus Date Posted: November 2, 2026 Closing Date: Continuous – application review begins November 19, 2026 Salary Information: Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience Monthly Type: 11 Month Full/Part-Time: Part Time – Full Time Equivalency (FTE): 0.05 FTE per position Tenure/Non-Tenure: Non-Tenure Temp/Perm: Temporary Other Conditions: First review of applications to begin November 19, 2026. Annually renewable subject to satisfactory performance and funding availability, to begin approximately December 2026. Duties & Responsibilities: Responsible for curriculum, administration, and evaluation in medical undergraduate, graduate, and post-graduate education. Assists with the development, support, and attainment of goals and objectives to support the Hematology / Oncology fellowship program. Teach medical students, graduate students, post-graduate residents, fellows, and faculty, providing formative feedback and upholding professionalism. Demonstrate commitment to the delivery of safe, equitable, high-quality, cost-effective, patient-centered care. Administer and maintain an educational environment conducive to educating fellows. Regularly participate in organized clinical discussions, rounds, journal clubs, and conferences. Participate in faculty development. Conduct and promote research and scholarly activities. Contribute to scholarly activities required for accreditation. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Assistant Professor MD degree or equivalent medical degree from an accredited medical school. Board certification or qualification to become board certified in Hematology and/or Medical Oncology through the American Board of Internal Medicine. Valid Hawaii Medical license by date of hire. Demonstrated ability in teaching and patient care. Excellent communication skills, written and spoken. Excellent organizational skills. Associate Professor Same as Assistant Plus Minimum of four (4) years at the rank of Assistant professor or four (4) years of other medical experience or minimum of one year at the rank of Associate Professor at another accredited medical school. Board certification in Hematology and/or Medical Oncology through the American Board of Internal Medicine. Proven ability to teach medical students, residents, or fellows. Evidence of excellent patient care in a collaborative environment. Evidence of effective research and scholarly activity (i.e., recent publications in peer-reviewed journals or regional/national presentations), or medical education administration. Experience in academic and/or clinical program administration. Evidence of excellent team building and interpersonal skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Experience functioning in a complex system of multiple organizations and stakeholders. Familiarity with Liaison Committee on Medical Education (LCME) and Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) requirements. Desirable Qualifications: Demonstrated experience with curriculum development and evaluation. Eligibility for clinical privileges at The Queen’s Health Systems or Hawaii Pacific Health. Familiarity with curriculum development and evaluation, provider of educational activities as required by the LCME, ACGME, and the Accreditation Council for Continuing Medical Education (ACCME). To Apply: Click on the “ Apply ” button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach the required documents: Cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, Curriculum Vitae Names and contact information of five professional references, Copy of U.S. Board Certificates and current U.S. medical license or Official transcripts from medical school plus certificates of completion from residency training and current U.S. medical license. Copies of transcripts are accepted when used instead of current U.S. board certification or current U.S. medical license. However, if used for verification, original transcripts are required upon hire. The application will be considered incomplete if materials are unreadable. Late or incomplete applications will not be considered. Inquiries: Scott K. Kuwada, MD – skkuwada@hawaii.edu Maria Inong - minong@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
