    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5436746/lecturer-csd600": {
      "title": "Lecturer (CSD600)",
      "description": "Lecturer (CSD600) Salary $0.00 Semi-Monthly Location UH Manoa - JABSOM, Kaka'ako - Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01709 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Division Communication Sciences and Disorders Opening Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: Lecturer Description Title: Lecturer Position Number: Pending Hiring Unit: UHM School of Medicine - Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders Location: JABSOM Kaka’ako – Goldbond Building Date Posted: August 4, 2026 Closing Date: Continuous recruitment, first review August 19, 2026 Salary Information: Minimum LA $2,053 per credit hour Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: Fall 2026, part-time, for lecturer candidate pool, non-tenurial, assignments as needed, contingent on availability of funds, satisfactory performance, and actual staffing requirements. To begin August 24, 2026, pending position clearance and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities Teach courses in the Dept. of Communication Sciences and Disorders (CSD) including and not limited to CSD600-Research Methods. Other scholarly duties as assigned. Assistant Professor Minimum Qualifications: PhD or EdD degree in Communication Sciences and Disorders or related field from college or university of recognized standing, with major work in CSD. A PhD candidate who has completed all requirements of the degree except dissertation (“all but dissertation” or “ABD”) are also eligible; however, if all degree requirements are not fulfilled within a two-year period, the contract of the individual will not be renewed. Demonstrated experience and expertise in research. Demonstrated ability as a teacher. Poise and good address for meeting, collaborating, and conferring with others. Demonstrated scholarly achievement. Associate Professor Minimum Qualifications: Same as Assistant Professor level, as well as: A minimum of four years of full-time college or university teaching at the rank of assistant professor or equivalent, with evidence of increasing professional maturity. Scholarly achievement judged competent and adequate for the rank in comparison with peers active in the same field at major research universities. Continued evidence of participation in the scholarly and academic affairs of a university or other appropriate organization, or in an appropriate organization, or in an appropriate professional society or organization, or in other appropriate job-related service activities. Demonstrated ability to plan and organize assigned activities, including the supervision of work of assistants when appropriate. Ability to service as a role model for students and junior colleagues. Desirable Qualifications: Experience in working in a multicultural setting. To Apply: Submit original cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, CV, copies of licenses and certifications, names and contact information of 5 professional references (including email addresses) and official transcripts (or original documentation from the institution confirming degree). Copies of transcripts are accepted; however, original transcripts are required upon hire. Please note that incomplete applications will not be considered. Address: Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders University of Hawaii at Manoa, John A. Burns School of Medicine 677 Ala Moana Blvd., Suite 625 Honolulu, HI 96813 Inquiries: Keith Yamase; 808-692-1583; keithy@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - John A. Burns School of Medicine Address 651 Ilalo Street Honolulu, Hawaii, 96813 Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/4160354/lecturer-dental-hygiene": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Dental Hygiene)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Dental Hygiene) Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01655 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - School of Nursing and Dental Hygiene - Dental Hygiene Opening Date 02/18/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: 0004LECB Description Title: Lecturer (Dental Hygiene) Position Number: 0004LECB Hiring Unit: UH at Manoa School of Nursing and Dental Hygiene Location: Honolulu Date Posted: February 18, 2026 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Applicable Minimum for the Academic Year Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer applicant pool for Academic Year 2026 - 2027. Positions are part-time, temporary, non-tenure, and contingent upon course offerings, sufficient student enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. Must be available to teach courses during the day, evening, weekend, and/or via distance learning/on- & off-campus (e.g., clinical settings), as needed. To know more about the UH at Manoa School of Nursing and Dental Hygiene , go to: https://nursing.hawaii.edu/dental-hygiene-bachelor/ Duties and Responsibilities: Under general supervision, design, deliver, and assess instruction in terms of student learning outcomes; teach assigned courses in the undergraduate dental hygiene program; develop and/or update course content and materials; use teaching strategies to meet the college's diverse students learning needs; submit annual self-assessment; mentor and assist students; complete grades on a timely basis; attend faculty meetings and other duties that the supervisor assigns. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Dental Hygiene from an accredited college or university; with five (5) years of experience in area of teaching responsibility; Current unrestricted Dental Hygienist; Engaged in professional practice with a similar patient population and level of patient acuity for the purpose of supervising nursing students; Demonstrated ability to teach effectively and to direct group discussion; Demonstrated ability to provide clinical supervision to dental hygiene students. Desirable Qualifications: Previous experience with a bachelor's level dental hygiene curriculum. Previous teaching experience with teaching and/or supervising undergraduate dental hygiene students including didactic and clinical courses. To Apply: Click on the “Apply” button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and upload the required documents. Required documents include: Cover letter indicating interest in the position and how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; Current resume / curriculum vitae; Names and contact information (including email address) of at least three (3) professional references; Transcripts showing degree and coursework appropriate to the position (original official transcripts will be required at the time of hire). NOTE: Application will not be considered if NEOGOV Online application is incomplete or any of the required documents are not included or are unreadable. If this is your first time applying for a position using NEOGOV, please create a new account. Inquiries: Kristine Osada, Program Administrator for the Department of Dental Hygiene; kmsato@hawaii.edu Corie O. Fulgencio-Arre, HR Specialist; mcfa@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5456410/lecturer-economics": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Economics)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Economics) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2026-01837 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Social Sciences - Economics Opening Date 08/20/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (Economics) Hiring Unit: College of Social Sciences, Department of Economics Location: UH at Manoa Date Posted: 08/20/2026 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum Salary $2,053.00 per credit hour, in accordance with the applicable UHPA lecturer fee schedule. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool for Spring 2027 and future semesters, day and/or evening courses, including Outreach extension and summer courses. Courses are primarily online asynchronous; however, needs may occasionally arise for online synchronous or in-person courses. For online asynchronous course teaching, the College of Social Sciences will require training in advance. Contingent upon registration, position availability, course offerings, departmental need, and funding. Applicants may refer to the list of Economics (ECON) courses in the UH Manoa Catalog: https://catalog.manoa.hawaii.edu/content.php?filter%5B27%5D=ECON&filter%5B29%5D=&filter%5Bcourse_type%5D=-1&filter%5Bkeyword%5D=&filter%5B32%5D=1&filter%5Bcpage%5D=1&cur_cat_oid=4&expand=&navoid=949&search_database=Filter&filter%5Bexact_match%5D=1#acalog_template_course_filter Positions are part-time, non-tenure for lecturer candidate pool. Because UH Manoa employment is limited to individuals residing in Hawai'i, lecturers are required to reside in and teach from Hawai'i. For information about the department, visit https://economics.hawaii.edu/ . Duties and Responsibilities To teach various undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Economics. Other related duties, including meeting course requirements as established by the department, preparing course syllabus, grading, and maintaining weekly office hours. Minimum Qualifications M.A. in Economics or an appropriate related field from a college or university of recognized standing, with the major work in field or related field in which the instructional assignment is made or duties performed; Evidence of ability to teach effectively, direct group discussions, and/or to provide clinical supervision; Demonstrated ability of professionalism in meeting and conferring with others. Desirable Qualifications Ph.D. in Economics or an appropriate related field. Teaching experience at the college or university level. Experience teaching online (asynchronous and/or synchronous) courses. Experience using learning management systems such as Brightspace by D2L or Lamaku at UH. To Apply When applying, send electronic application materials via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) to the Department of Economics with the file recipient as econ@hawaii.edu and the expiration timer set to 14 days. letter of application, curriculum vitae, copy of transcripts (official transcripts will be required at time of hire), and contact information of three (3) professional references. Incomplete applications will not be accepted. Application materials will not be returned. Inquiries Department of Economics, econ@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/2570924/lecturer-engineering": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Engineering)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Engineering) Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2019-01067 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Engineering Opening Date 09/12/2019 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Description Title: Lecturer Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Engineering Location: Manoa Campus Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $1,911 per credit hour, commensurate with qualifications and experience. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: Positions are part-time, non-tenure for lecturer applicant pool, for future semesters, dependent upon course and staff needs and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities To teach various courses in the Department of Civil & Environmental Engineering, Mechanical Engineering and Electrical Engineering. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's, Master's, Ph.D. or D.V.M. in appropriate field from a college or university of recognized standing. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness. If qualified applicants are not available, those not meeting minimum requirements may be considered. Desirable Qualifications College teaching experience. To Apply: Submit the following to the appropriate Department listed below: 1) send cover letter of interest 2) curriculum vitae 3) official transcripts and 4) contact information for at least three (3) professional references. When applying, address letter to: Name of Department, Campus Building, University of Hawaii, 2540 Dole Street, Honolulu, HI 96822 Attn: Lecturer Pool. The names of departments/programs and campus buildings are: Civil & Environmental Engineering Dept (CEE), Holmes Hall 383 // Electrical Engineering(EE), Holmes Hall 483// Mechanical Engineering (ME), Holmes Hall 302 Inquiries: (CEE) Phil Ooi, Dept chair; email: ooi@hawaii.edu (ME) Joe Brown, Dept chair; email:jjbrown@hawaii.edu (EE) Wayne Shiroma, Dept chair; email: wayne.shiroma@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/4759993/lecturer-english": {
      "title": "Lecturer (English)",
      "description": "Lecturer (English) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2024-02736 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of English Opening Date 12/12/2024 Position Number: LECTURER Description Title: Lecturer (English) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, English Dept Location: UH Manoa Date Posted: December 12, 2024 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $1,978 per credit hour Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in the department adjunct lecturer pool for Fall 2025, Spring 2026, and Summer 2026. Mainly part-time employment, contingent on approval to fill, course offerings, availability of funds, and sufficient enrollment. Appointments offered on a semester basis. Duties and Responsibilities Teach primarily lower-division courses: ENG100 Composition I; ENG100A Composition 1 (Honors); ENG200 Composition II; ENG209 Business Writing, ENG270 - 276 Introduction to Literature (emphases on literary history, genre, culture, creative writing, or rhetoric). Minimum Qualifications MA or MFA degree in English or appropriate field from a college or university of recognized standing; Ability to teach effectively, direct group discussions; Professionalism in meeting and conferring with others Desirable Qualifications Ph.D. in English or other appropriate field; Experience teaching first-year writing, writing intensive, and/or introductory literature courses at the college or university level; Evidence of scholarly or professional activity. To Apply: Submit cover letter, noting which semester(s) and English course(s) you are applying for and explaining how you meet the minimum and desirable qualifications; CV; transcripts (copies are acceptable; official transcripts will be required at time of hire); names, titles, and contact information of three professional references (including phone numbers and email addresses); one-page pedagogy statement, one sample syllabus, and summarized student evaluation data for appropriate courses if available. Please submit materials to enghi@hawaii.edu. Inquiries: enghi@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ . Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai’i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai’i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ . Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/3821572/lecturer-field-supervisor-elementary": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Field Supervisor), Elementary",
      "description": "Lecturer (Field Supervisor), Elementary Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2022-01880 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Education Opening Date 12/01/2022 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: Lecturer Description Title: Lecturer (Field Supervisor) Hiring Unit: College of Education, Institute for Teacher Education – Elementary Location: Manoa Date Posted: December 1, 2022 Closing Date: Continuous Salary: Minimum of $1,733 per credit hour Other conditions: Lecturer applicant pool for future semesters; temporary, part-time work, as needed, contingent upon student enrollment, position availability and funding. May be for day, evening, or weekend offerings on- and off-campus. Selectee is required to complete the COE New Faculty orientation in the first year and pass a criminal background check and Title IX training. Duties and Responsibilities Coordinate field placements with principals and teachers. Supervise, mentor and evaluate students in field-based settings in secondary classrooms. Conduct field experience seminars and student teaching seminars. Evaluate candidates' lesson plans and field-based program assignments. Conduct midterm and end-of-semester conferences. Participate in collaborative relationships with mentor teachers, school administrators, and staff. Provide service to the department, university and broader community. Minimum Qualifications Earned master's degree in Education, or equivalent combination of graduate education and experience. Working knowledge of national content standards, Hawaii Content and Performance Standards III, InTASC Standards, and Common Core Standards. Three years full-time K-12 classroom teaching experience, as teacher of record, with at least two years of K-6 teaching experience, as teacher of record. Experience working with various student populations. Desirable Qualifications Successful post-secondary teaching experience. Experience working with native Hawaiian populations. Experience teaching on-line courses. Experience with school/university partnerships. Experience mentoring students in field settings. Experience in field-based, standards-based teacher education. Experience working with special education students and/or multilingual learners. To Apply: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Documents include: (1) cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) name and contact information of three (3) professional references and (4) official transcripts (copies of official transcripts are acceptable; however, original official transcripts will be required at the time of hire.) Incomplete applications will not be considered. The application will be considered incomplete if material is unreadable. Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NEOGOV, you will need to create an account. Inquiries: Institute for Teacher Education Elementary Program; kk29@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/2306857/lecturer-french": {
      "title": "Lecturer (French)",
      "description": "Lecturer (French) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2018-01033 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of Languages&Literatures of Europe & the Americas Opening Date 11/01/2018 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (French) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: Coll of Arts, Languages & Letters, French and Italian Div, Dept of Lang and Lit of Europe and the Americas Location: Manoa Date Posted: November 01, 2018 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $2,053 per credit hour Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in part-time lecturer pool for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. The Division of French and Italian offers student-focused instruction with an active program of extracurricular activities to support learning. Contingent on course offerings, sufficient enrollment, position clearance and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities Teach first-year, second-year and third-year French classes. Attend pilot classes as assigned. Minimum Qualifications M.A. or equivalent degree in French; high level fluency in French and English; experience teaching French at the college or university level; excellent student evaluations Desirable Qualifications An engaged approach to language and cultural learning demonstrated by any suitable combination of the following: evidence of student-oriented and innovative instruction; evidence of contributions to student learning and cultural activities. To Apply: Submit a letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, resume, evidence of excellent student evaluations, and the names, address, telephone numbers, and e-mails of 3 professional references (do not send letters of recommendation at this time), and transcripts (copies acceptable; however, official transcripts are required upon hiring). Email all application materials as a single pdf file as follows: LastNameFRlecturer to Dr. Louis Bousquet, Chair of the Division of French and Italian, at lb2010@hawaii.edu. Inquiries: Dr. Louis Bousquet; lb2010@hawaii.edu Inquiries: Louis Bousquet; 808-956-4185; lb2010@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ . Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai’i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai’i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ . Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/2306869/lecturer-german": {
      "title": "Lecturer (German)",
      "description": "Lecturer (German) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2018-01035 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of Languages&Literatures of Europe & the Americas Opening Date 04/07/2016 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (German) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, German Div of the Dept of Lang and Lit of Europe and the Americas Location: Manoa Date Posted: April 07, 2016 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $2,053 per credit hour; commensurate with experience. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Mainly part-time employment, contingent on approval to fill, course offerings (ranging from 3 to 12 credits), position clearance, availability of funds, and sufficient enrollment. Appointments offered on a semester basis. Duties and Responsibilities Teach first-year, second-year and third-year German classes. Teaching load to be determined (between 1 and 4 courses per semester). Minimum Qualifications M.A. or equivalent degree in German; high level proficiency in German and English; experience teaching German at the college or university level; excellent student evaluations. Desirable Qualifications Evidence of student-oriented and innovative instruction. To Apply: Email letter of application, résumé, evidence of excellent student evaluations, and the names, addresses, telephone numbers, transcripts (copies are acceptable; official transcripts will be required at time of hire) and e-mails of three references (do not send letters of recommendation at this time) to Dr. Maryann Overstreet, German Chair, Department of Languages and Literatures of Europe and the Americas, overst@hawaii.edu. Inquiries: Dr. Maryann Overstreet, German Chair; 808-956-4172; overst@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ . Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai’i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai’i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ . Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
