      "description": "Lecturer (Maori) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2021-01091 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of Indo-Pacific Languages & Literatures Opening Date 10/21/2021 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: Pending Description Title: Lecturer (Maori) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, Dept. of lndo-Pacific Languages and Literatures Location: Manoa Date Posted: 10/22/2021 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $2,053 per credit hour; commensurate with experience. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Contingent on course offerings, sufficient enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. The candidate must work in Hawai'i. Duties and Responsibilities 1. To teach basic Maori language skill courses in the target language. Maintain office hours and work with other language programs in integrating teaching efforts. Minimum Qualifications 1. B.A. with emphasis on Education/Bilingual Education, Linguistics, ESL, Second Language/Foreign Language Teaching, or closely related fields; high level oral and written fluency in target language and English. Desirable Qualifications 1. Demonstrated evidence of successful teaching; university level teaching experience of the target language; experience in target language curriculum development; evidence of prior or pending research and/or publications on target language. To Apply: Email cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications. Include resume/CV, transcripts (copies are acceptable; official transcripts will be required at time of hire) and contact information for 3 references to stakeo@hawaii.edu. EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a 