    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/2306994/lecturer-portuguese-spanish": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Portuguese/Spanish)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Portuguese/Spanish) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2018-01040 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Languages, Linguistics & Literature Opening Date 05/20/2014 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (Portuguese/Spanish) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, Languages and Literatures of Europe and the Americas Location: 1890 East-West Road, Moore 483 Date Posted: May 20, 2014 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $1,911per credit hour; commensurate with experience. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool for Fall 2025, Spring 2026, and Summer 2026 . Mainly part-time employment, contingent on approval to fill, course offerings (ranging from 3 to 12 credits), position clearance, availability of funds, and sufficient enrollment. Appointment offered on a semester basis. Duties and Responsibilities Teaching first-year, second-year, and third-year Spanish or Portuguese courses under supervision. Minimum Qualifications M.A. or equivalent degree in Spanish or Portuguese, linguistics, education, journalism, film/cultural studies or related field; high level fluency in Spanish or Portuguese, and English; experience teaching Spanish or Portuguese at the college or university level; excellent student evaluations. Desirable Qualifications Evidence of student-oriented and innovative instruction. To Apply: Email letter of application, résumé, evidence of excellent student evaluations, transcripts (copies are acceptable; official transcripts will be required at time of hire), and the names, addresses, telephone numbers, and e-mails of three references (do not send letters of recommendation at this time) to Dr. Benito Quintana, Spanish Chair, Department of Languages and Literatures of Europe and the Americas, benitoq@hawaii.edu. Inquiries: Dr. Benito Quintana; 808-956-8796; benitoq@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/ offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/ titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/ offices/eeo/accommodation- request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website https://www.governmentjobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/4249069/lecturer-private-school-leadership-program": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Private School Leadership Program)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Private School Leadership Program) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2023-02154 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Education Division Educational Administration Opening Date 10/18/2023 Position Number: Lecturer Description Title: Lecturer (Private School Leadership Program) Hiring Unit: College of Education, Department of Educational Foundations (EDEF) and Educational Administration (EDEA) Location: Manoa Date Posted: October 18, 2023 Closing Date: Continuous Other conditions: Lecturer applicant pool for future semesters within the Private School Leadership (PSL) Master’s degree program; temporary, part-time work, as needed, contingent upon student enrollment, position availability and funding. May be for day, evening, or weekend offerings on- and off-campus. Selectee is required to complete the COE New Faculty orientation in the first year and pass a criminal background check and Title IX training. Looking for individuals with specific K12 work or educational experience to teach the following coursework: Education Law Educational Inquiry Introduction to Educational Administration Human Resources Management Principals of School Leadership Teacher Development and Evaluation Seminar in Governance and Policy Educational Finance Culture and Community Seminar in Funding Private Education Non-Profit Management Duties and Responsibilities Teach various undergraduate and graduate level courses in the Departments of Educational Foundation (EDEF) and Educational Administration (EDEA). Prepare course syllabi that meets COE accreditation standards. Mentor and assist students. Complete grades on a timely basis. Attend faculty meetings and other duties that the supervisor assigns. Minimum Qualifications A Master's degree in Education or related field from a college or university of recognized standing, with the major work in the field in which the instructional assignment is made; equivalent experience in a relevant area will be considered (2 years minimum). Evidence of ability to teach effectively and to direct group discussions. Poise and good address for meeting and conferring with others. Ability to travel independently to various geographical locations in a timely manner. Requirement may be fulfilled by a valid Hawai'i Driver's License (class 3), comparable driver's license, or other means of transportation which meets position needs. Any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Desirable Qualifications Experience teaching at the College level. Experience in a K12 school environment setting as a teacher, advisor, or administrator role. To Apply: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Documents include: (1) cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) name and contact information of three (3) professional references and (4) official transcripts (copies of official transcripts are acceptable; however, original official transcripts will be required at the time of hire.) Incomplete applications will not be considered. The application will be considered incomplete if material is unreadable. Note: If you have not applied for a position before using NEOGOV, you will need to create an account. Inquiries: 808-956-7913 EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/3643019/lecturer-religion": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Religion)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Religion) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2022-00955 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of Religion & Ancient Civilizations Opening Date 07/19/2022 Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer (Religion) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, Department of Religion & Ancient Civilizations Location: Manoa Date Posted: July 19, 2022 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $2,053 per credit hour. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Positions are part-time, temporary, non-tenure, and contingent upon course offerings, sufficient student enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities 1. Teach undergraduate courses in Religion, Classics, and/or Latin at the lower and upper division levels. 2. Other related duties, including meeting course requirements as established by the department, preparing course syllabus, grading, maintaining weekly office hours. 3. Other duties as required. Minimum Qualifications 1. Master's degree in the academic study of religion or related field, recent approaches to religious studies and teaching experience. Desirable Qualifications 1. Ph.D. in the academic study of Religion, Classics, and/or Latin or related field or equivalent appropriate academic or professional training. To Apply: Submit cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and/or desirable qualifications, curriculum vitae, names and contact information (including e-mail address) of at least 2 professional references, and official transcripts (copies are acceptable, however, original and official transcripts will be required at the time of hire) to relclas@hawaii.edu via UH FileDropService at https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop with the expiration timer for the file upload set to 14 days. Application materials become the property of the University of Hawaii at Manoa and will not be returned. Address: Jonathan Pettit, Chair/ Department of Religion University of Hawaii at Manoa Sakamaki A-311 2530 Dole Street Honolulu, HI 96822 Inquiries: Jonathan Pettit, jeep@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination on the basis of race, sex, gender identity and expression, age, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, disability, genetic information, marital status, breastfeeding, income assignment for child support, arrest and court record (except as permissible under State law), sexual orientation, domestic or sexual violence victim status, national guard absence, or status as a covered veteran. For more information or inquiries regarding these policies, please refer to the following link: http://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/eeo-coordinators/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5158496/lecturer-school-counseling": {
      "title": "Lecturer (School Counseling)",
      "description": "Lecturer (School Counseling) Location UH Manoa - College of Ed, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2025-02530 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Education Division Educational Psychology Opening Date 12/02/2025 Position Number: PENDING Description Title: Lecturer (School Counseling) Hiring Unit: College of Education / Department of Education Psychology Location: Manoa Date Posted: December 2, 2025 Closing Date: Continuous Other conditions: Lecturer applicant pool for future semesters; temporary, part-time work, as needed, contingent upon student enrollment, position availability and funding. May be for day, evening, or weekend offerings on- and off-campus. Selectee is required to complete the COE New Faculty orientation in the first year and pass a criminal background check and Title IX training. The School Counseling and Rehabilitation Counseling programs prepare graduate students to become licensed professional counselors, including school counselors and rehabilitation counselors who provide responsive, evidence-based services in PK-12, rehabilitation counseling and community mental health settings. Instruction in these programs incorporates multiple delivery modalities—including face-to-face, online synchronous, and online asynchronous formats—and emphasizes the preparation of practitioners who can meet professional, ethical, and accreditation standards. Duties and Responsibilities Teach various graduate level counseling courses in School and Rehabilitation Counseling. Prepare course syllabi that meets COE accreditation expectations and Hawai‘i state licensing standards. Mentor and assist students. Complete grades on a timely basis. Attend faculty meetings and other duties that the supervisor assigns. Minimum Qualifications A Master's degree in Counseling or related field from an accredited college or university of recognized standing, with work as a counselor; equivalent experience in a relevant area will be considered. An active license or certification in the counseling area of expertise (e.g., School Counselor, Mental Health Counselor, Rehabilitation Counselor), or related field, or the ability to attain a relevant license or certification within 6 months to 1 year of hire. Evidence of ability to teach effectively and to direct group discussions. Professionalism when meeting and conferring with others. Any equivalent combination of education and/or professional work experience which provides the required education, knowledge, skills and abilities as indicated. Desirable Qualifications Doctorate in Counselor Education or a closely related field from an accredited college or university of recognized standing. Experience teaching in higher education at the undergraduate and graduate level. Experience mentoring and supervising Counseling students in the field. Experience teaching online. To Apply: Click on the \"Apply\" button on the top right corner of the screen to complete an application and attach required documents. Documents include: (1) cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) name and contact information of three (3) professional references and (4) official transcripts (copies of official transcripts are acceptable; however, original official transcripts will be required at the time of hire.) Late, incomplete, or unreadable application materials will not be considered. Please REDACT references to social security numbers and birth date on submitted documents. All items become the property of the University of Hawaii and will not be returned. NOTE: If you have not applied for a position before using NEOGOV, you will need to create an account. The maximum file size to upload/attach is 10 MB. If the attachment is larger than 10 MB, please split the file and upload it as a supplemental attachment. Inquiries: 808-956-7775 EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/4097094/lecturer-school-of-cinematic-arts": {
      "title": "Lecturer (School of Cinematic Arts)",
      "description": "Lecturer (School of Cinematic Arts) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2023-01283 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - School of Cinematic Arts Opening Date 06/26/2023 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer ( School of Cinematic Arts ) Position Number: pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages, and Letters, School of Cinematic Arts Location: Manoa Date Posted: June 26, 2023 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum salary: $2,053 per credit hour Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool beginning Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Positions are part-time, temporary, non-tenure, and contingent upon course offerings, sufficient student enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. Duties and Responsibilities To teach various 3-credit courses in screenwriting, film production, computer animation, and critical studies. Other related duties, including meeting course requirements as established by the department, preparing course syllabus, grading, maintaining weekly office hours. Minimum Qualifications M.A. or M.F.A. in appropriate field or professional or teaching experience. Desirable Qualifications Ph.D. in appropriate field or professional or teaching experience. Prior university teaching experience and/or demonstrated teaching ability. To Apply: Submit the following: (1) cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) media portfolio (where applicable); (4) names of 3 professional references; and (5) official transcripts (copies are acceptable, originals will be required at time of hire) through the University Filedrop System . Send application materials to acham@hawaii.edu . Address: School of Cinematic Arts Attn: Lecturer Pool 2550 Campus Road, Crawford 210 Honolulu, HI 96822 Inquiries: Chair, Christine Acham, acham@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai’i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ . Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai’i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai’i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ . Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5470673/lecturer-school-of-cinematic-arts-3d-animation": {
      "title": "LECTURER (School of Cinematic Arts, 3D Animation)",
      "description": "LECTURER (School of Cinematic Arts, 3D Animation) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number LECTURER Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - School of Cinematic Arts Opening Date 09/02/2026 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: LECTURER Description Title: Lecturer (School of Cinematic Arts, 3D Animation) Position Number: Pending Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, School of Cinematic Arts Location: Manoa Date Posted: September 03, 2026 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum salary: $2,053 per credit hour Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in the lecturer pool beginning Spring 2027 and Summer 2027. Positions are part-time, temporary, non-tenure, and contingent upon course offerings, sufficient student enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. Appointments are offered on a semester basis. Duties and Responsibilities Teach various 3-credit courses in 3D animation. Other related duties, including meeting course requirements as established by the department, preparing course syllabus, grading, and maintaining weekly office hours. Minimum Qualifications: MA or MFA degree in Animation or appropriate field from a college or university of recognized standing; Proficiency in industry-standard software suites and specialized applications, including: a. Unreal Engine, Maya and Adobe Creative Suite, and b. ZBrush, Substance Painter, Maxon Cinema 4D or comparable software. Evidence of ability to teach effectively and direct group discussions; Demonstrated ability of professionalism in meeting and conferring with others. Desirable Qualifications: Teaching experience at the college or university level; Professional industry experience and accomplishment in 3D animation as demonstrated through the creation, direction, and collaboration of projects that include 3D animation; Demonstrated knowledge and experience across the 3D animation production pipeline, including pre-visualization, modeling, texturing, rigging, character animation, visual effects (VFX), lighting, and rendering, with advanced expertise in one or more of these areas. To Apply: Submit the following: (1) cover letter indicating how you satisfy the minimum and desirable qualifications; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) media portfolio (where applicable); (4) names of 3 professional references; and (5) official transcripts (copies are acceptable, originals will be required at time of hire) through the University’s Filedrop service, https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ . Send application materials to acham@hawaii.edu . Inquiries: Christine Acham, Department Chair, acham@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5015013/lecturer-second-language-studies": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Second Language Studies)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Second Language Studies) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2025-01570 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - CALL - Department of Second Language Studies Opening Date 07/21/2025 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: LECTURER Description Title: Lecturer (Second Language Studies) Hiring Unit: College of Arts, Languages & Letters, Linguistics Location: Manoa Date Posted: 07/21/2025 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum $2,053 per credit hour; commensurate with experience. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in the department lecturer pool for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and Summer 2027. Contingent on course offerings, sufficient enrollment, position clearance, and availability of funds. Appointment based on a semester basis. This is not for programs in the Hawaii English Language Program or English Language Institute. Duties and Responsibilities Teach primarily Second Language Studies courses such as undergraduate major courses or introductory/core graduate courses as needed; Hold regularly scheduled office hours to advise students in courses taught. Minimum Qualifications MA in Second Language Studies, Applied Linguistics, English as a Second Language or related discipline (for undergraduate courses); PhD in Second Language Studies, Applied Linguistics, or related discipline (for graduate courses); Experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate level SLS, applied linguistics, or language teacher education (or related) courses. Desirable Qualifications PhD with specialization in area covered by SLS courses [e.g., second language acquisition, language learning technology, sociolinguistics, language education, second language processing, pedagogical grammar]; College-level classroom experience developing curriculum for second language studies or similar courses; Familiarity with the UHM SLS undergraduate and graduate programs. To Apply Send a letter of application indicating which courses you would be qualified to teach and how you meet the minimum and desired qualifications, CV, names and contact information for three referees, and transcripts (copies acceptable at time of application; however, original transcripts required upon hire) by email to SLSCHAIR@hawaii.edu with \"Lecturer\" in the subject line. Additional information such as teaching evaluations may be requested during the review process Inquiries Dr. Betsy Gilliland, Chair; egillila@hawaii.edu EEO, Clery Act, ADA The University of Hawai'i is an Equal Opportunity Institution and is committed to a policy of nondiscrimination in employment, including on the basis of veteran and disability status. For more information, visit: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/policies/ Employment is contingent on satisfying employment eligibility verification requirements of the Immigration Reform and Control Act of 1986; reference checks of previous employers; and for certain positions, criminal history record checks. In accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, annual campus crime statistics for the University of Hawai'i may be viewed at: https://www.hawaii.edu/titleix/help/campus-security/ , or a paper copy may be obtained upon request from the respective UH Campus Security or Administrative Services Office. Accommodation Request: The University of Hawai'i complies with the provisions of the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application and hiring process should contact the EEO coordinator directly. Determination on requests for reasonable accommodation will be made on a case-by-case basis. For further information, please refer to the following link: https://www.hawaii.edu/offices/eeo/accommodation-request/ Employer University of Hawaii Website http://workatuh.hawaii.edu"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/hawaiiedu/jobs/5058937/lecturer-social-sciences": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Social Sciences)",
      "description": "Lecturer (Social Sciences) Salary See Position Description Location UH Manoa, Honolulu, HI Job Type Part-Time Temporary Job Number 2025-01876 Department University of Hawai'i at Manoa - College of Social Sciences Opening Date 09/03/2025 Closing Date Continuous Position Number: pending Description Title: Lecturer Hiring Unit: College of Social Sciences Location: UH at Manoa Date Posted: 09/03/2025 Closing Date: Continuous Salary Information: Minimum Salary $1,978.00 per credit hour. Full Time/Part Time: Part Time Temporary/Permanent: Temporary Other Conditions: For placement in lecturer pool for current and future semesters, day and/or evening courses, including Outreach extension and summer courses. Contingent upon registration, position availability, course offerings, departmental need, and funding. Positions are part-time, non-tenure for lecturer candidate pool. Lecturers are required to reside in and teach from Hawaii. To know more about the College of Social Sciences, please visit: https://socialsciences.manoa.hawaii.edu/ Duties and Responsibilities To teach various courses in Anthropology, Economics, Ethnic Studies, Geography and Environment, the Manoa Academy, Political Science, Psychology, Public Administration Program, School of Communication and Information, Social Sciences, Sociology, Urban & Regional Planning, and Women, Gender and Sexuality Studies. Other related duties, include meeting course requirements as established by the department/program, preparing course syllabus, grading, maintaining weekly office hours. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree from a college or university of recognized standing, with the major work in field or related field in which the instructional assignment is made or duties performed; Evidence of ability to teach effectively, direct group discussions, and/or to provide clinical supervision; Demonstrated ability of professionalism in meeting and conferring with others. To Apply When applying, send hard copy application materials to the department or electronic application materials via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) using the departmental contact information indicated below. letter of application, curriculum vitae, copy of transcripts (official transcripts will be required at time of hire), and contact information of three (3) professional references. Incomplete applications will not be accepted. Application materials will not be returned. Anthropology Dept Inquiries: anthprog@hawaii.edu Phone: 808-956-7153 Website: anthropology.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy or electronic applications: Please contact anthprog@hawaii.edu for more information. Economics Dept Inquiries: econ@hawaii.edu Website: economics.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Department of Economics University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2424 Maile Way, Saunders Hall 542 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: mjs@hawaii.edu Ethnic Studies Dept Inquiries: eschair@hawaii.edu Website: ethnicstudies.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Ethnic Studies Department University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2560 Campus Road, George Hall 301 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: esdept@hawaii.edu Geography and Environment Inquiries: Elizabeth Tajima, Administrative Assistant Phone: 808-956-8465 Website: geography.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Geography and Environment University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2424 Maile Way, Saunders Hall 445 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: etajima3@hawaii.edu Manoa Academy Inquiries: Jaret Leong, jaretl@hawaii.edu Phone: 808-956-3687 Website: https://socialsciences.manoa.hawaii.edu/study-at-css/enrollment-pathways/manoa-academy/ Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Manoa Academy University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2500 Campus Road, Hawaii Hall 310 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: jaretl@hawaii.edu Political Science Dept Inquiries: Department Chair Professor Jonathan Goldberg-Hiller, polisci@hawaii.edu Phone: 808-956-8357 Website: politicalscience.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Political Science Department University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2424 Maile Way, Saunders Hall 640 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: polisci@hawaii.edu Psychology Dept Inquiries: Teri Imanaka, imanaka@hawaii.edu Website: psychology.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Psychology Department University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2530 Dole Street, Sakamaki C400 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: imanaka@hawaii.edu Public Administration Program Inquiries: pubadmin@hawaii.edu Website: puba.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Public Administration Program University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2424 Maile Way, Saunders Hall 631 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: pubadmin@hawaii.edu School of Communication and Information Inquiries: Please contact the desired program directly. Communication: Hanae Kramer, hanae@hawaii.edu Communicology: Krystyna Aune, krystyna@hawaii.edu Journalism: John Temple, john.temple@hawaii.edu Library & Information Science: Rich Gazan, gazan@hawaii.edu Peace & Conflict Education: Brien Hallett, bhallett@hawaii.edu Website: sci.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: School of Communication & Information University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool Communication 2550 Campus Road, Crawford 320 Honolulu, HI 96822 Communicology 2560 Campus Road, George 326 Honolulu, HI 96822 Journalism 2550 Campus Road, Crawford 320 Honolulu, HI 96822 Library & Information Science 2550 McCarthy Mall, Hamilton Library Room 002 Honolulu, HI 96822 Peace & Conflict Education 2424 Campus Road, Saunders 720 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: Communication: hanae@hawaii.edu Communicology: krystyna@hawaii.edu Journalism: john.temple@hawaii.edu Library & Information Science: gazan@hawaii.edu Peace & Conflict Education: bhallett@hawaii.edu Social Sciences Inquiries: cssadaa@hawaii.edu Website: socialsciences.manoa.hawaii.edu Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: cssadaa@hawaii.edu Sociology Dept Inquiries: socdept@hawaii.edu Phone: 808-956-7693 Website: sociology.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Sociology Department University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2424 Maile Way, Saunders Hall 247 Honolulu, HI 96822 Electronic applications. Send via UH FileDrop ( https://www.hawaii.edu/filedrop/ ) with the expiration timer set to 14 days. File recipient: socdept@hawaii.edu Urban and Regional Planning Dept Inquiries: Chrislyn DeMattos, cdematto@hawaii.edu Phone: 808-956-7381 Website: durp.manoa.hawaii.edu Hard copy applications. Mailing address: Urban and Regional Planning Department University of Hawaii at Manoa Attn: Lecturer Pool 2424 Maile Way, Saunders Hall 107 Honolulu, HI 96822 